Subject: [PATCH 66/67] =?UTF-8?q?Glint:=20profile=20tag=20survives=20redir?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ects=20=E2=80=94=20observe=20tab=20strips,=20tag=20by=20real=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?profile?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The profile-tag tracker now derives glintProfileTabs from each tab's actual
BrowserContext and observes every window's tab strip, so a link that redirects
into a new tab (SSO/OAuth window.open, target=_blank), a same-tab redirect, a
restored tab, or a tab opened in another window is badged immediately instead
of silently losing its tag. Display names persist in glintProfileNames so the
badge keeps its casing (and hashed colour) across restarts. The tracker is
re-armed per window from ExtensionSidePanelCoordinator (matched by extension
id, not display name) and tears down on profile destruction (ProfileObserver)
to avoid a dangling raw_ptr.

Adds a gated glint://open-profile/<name>/<url> bridge command (same
initiating-origin check as the other glint:// actions) so the panel — and
CDP-driven tests — can open a profile tab without the native palette.

